      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will affect reserved memory (MemTotal) and module loaded size (lsmod)\n\nIn our environment, the differences are as following:\n\n1. CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL\u003dy\nlsmod total size is 38580224 Bytes\nMemory: 1472924K/2097152K available (17088K kernel code, 2010K rwdata, 12400K rodata, 4224K init, 583K bss, 345532K reserved, 274432K cma-reserved)\n\n2. CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL\u003dn\nlsmod total size is 38039552 Bytes\nMemory: 1474076K/2097152K available (17088K kernel code, 2010K rwdata, 11204K rodata, 4224K init, 583K bss, 344380K reserved, 274432K cma-reserved)\n\nSo, we can calculate the memory difference\na. lsmod is 38580224 - 38039552 \u003d 528KB shrinked\nb. reserved is 345532K - 344380K \u003d 1152KB shrinked\nc. rodata is 12400K - 11204K \u003d 1196KB shrinked\n\nThen, the total memory difference is\n528KB + 1152KB + 1196KB \u003d 2876KB",
      "parentUuid": "e6a5e07c_fcb6f14d",
      "range": {
